{"name":"Dark Citron","hex":"#aabb00","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dark","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having an absolute or (more often) relative lack of light.","Extinguished."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A complete or (more often) partial absence of light.","Ignorance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dark"},{"term":"citron","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small citrus tree, Citrus medica."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a greenish yellow colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/citron"}],"entries":[{"title":"Citron","blocks":[{"text":"The citron is a large fragrant citrus fruit with a thick, coarse rind. It resembles a lemon, but is larger. It is one of the original citrus fruits from which all other citrus types developed through natural hybrid speciation or artificial hybridization. Though citron cultivars take on a wide variety of physical forms, they are all closely related genetically. It is used in Asian and Mediterranean cuisine, traditional medicines, perfume, and religious rituals and offerings. Hybrids of citrons with other citrus are commercially more prominent, most notably lemons and many limes, which were created using citrons."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Chinesische_Zedrat_Zitrone.jpg/330px-Chinesische_Zedrat_Zitrone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citron"},{"title":"Citron (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Citron is a dark lemon color similar to that of the fruit citron. As a tertiary color on the RYB color wheel, it is an equal mix of orange and green pigments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Citron.jpg/330px-Citron.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citron_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedi